    66	## 3. System B — new package `src/planner/runtime/`
    67	
    68	Files: `runtime/__init__.py`, `runtime/system_b.py`. (System A lands here in W3b — clean seam.)
    69	
    70	`class SystemB`:
    71	- Constructed with `conn_factory: Callable[[], sqlite3.Connection]`, `clock`, and the run
    72	  parameters `home`, `hermes_python` (from `minds.config`), plus `*, spawn: SpawnFn = spawn_popen`
    73	  and `role_default` (the worker skill, e.g. `config.worker_skill`). The `spawn` seam is what the
    74	  unit tests inject `FakeGateway.spawn` through.
    75	- Holds ONE `MindQueue[tuple[str, str]]` **keyed on `ticket_id`**, run callable `self._run`.
    76	- `set_off(ticket_id: str, role: str, prompt: str) -> None`: `self._queue.submit(ticket_id, (role, prompt))`.
    77	- `wait_idle(timeout=None) -> bool`: delegates to `self._queue.wait_idle` (test helper).
    78	
    79	**Why key on `ticket_id` (not `session_key`):** one mind == one ticket, so `ticket_id ↔
    80	session_key` is 1:1 and stable. Keying the queue on `ticket_id` makes step-0 and step-N of the
    81	same ticket share a key, so the queue serializes them — this **subsumes W1's "System B must
    82	serialize kickoff itself"** carry-forward (there is no two-step-0-with-no-key race, because both
    83	step-0 runs carry the same `ticket_id` key). It also preserves the exact correctness the queue
    84	exists for: at most one in-flight resume of a given durable `session_key` (the gateway's `4009`
    85	busy-guard is per-process only), because all resumes of a session come from set-offs of its one
    86	ticket, which the key serializes. The run callable resolves the CURRENT `session_key` at execution
    87	time — satisfying carry-forward (b).
    88	
    89	`self._run(ticket_id: str, item: tuple[str, str]) -> None` — the serialized body per set-off:
    90	1. **Start write (single door):** `set_run_status(conn, ticket_id, status=agent_working,
    91	   worker=role, now=now)`.
    92	2. **Resolve current key at execution time:** re-read `chat_session_key` from the DB now (NOT
    93	   captured at `set_off`). `key = None` ⇒ kickoff/step-0 (`session.create`); else resume.
    94	3. **Capture the expected gating field** from the pre-run state: `expected =
    95	   GATING_FIELD.get(pre_state)` (needs_review/done/dropped ⇒ None).
    96	4. **Run:** `result = run_step(key, role, prompt, on_event=None, home=self._home,
    97	   hermes_python=self._python, spawn=self._spawn)`.
    98	5. **Map RunResult → end status:**
    99	   - `result.status == "complete"` ⇒ run the **proposal-present invariant**: re-read the ticket;
   100	     `present = expected is not None and fields[expected].proposal is not None`;
   101	     present ⇒ `awaiting_approval`, absent ⇒ `errored` ("agent left no proposal — you haven't done
   102	     your job", surfaced in the event payload).
   103	   - `result.status in {"interrupted", "errored"}` ⇒ `errored` (surface `result.error`). No
   104	     proposal check (the run did not finish its step).
   105	6. **End write (single door):** `set_run_status(conn, ticket_id, status=<mapped>, worker=None,
   106	   session_key=result.session_key, now=now)` — one atomic UPDATE writes status + cleared worker +
   107	   the resolved durable key together, so a later step resumes the right session.
   108	
   109	**Proposal-present invariant vs. auto-accept — documented seam (W3b).** Today `plan propose`
   110	auto-accepts a gating proposal when below ceiling (`resolution.decide_file_proposal` →
   111	`_accept_gating_proposal`), which advances state and clears the proposal. System B is **not** wired
   112	to real runs in W3a (System A drives it, = W3b), so this interaction cannot occur yet; the unit
   113	tests arrange the DB proposal state directly through the fake gateway. When W3b reworks the gate so
   114	`propose` always parks (the code then owns auto-approve), the literal "proposal present on the
   115	expected gating field" invariant becomes exact. Flagged here and in the report; no code hedge in
   116	W3a (keep the literal invariant per the ticket's wording).
   117	
   118	**System B is dormant in W3a:** nothing in the running server calls `set_off` (that wiring is
   119	System A = W3b). It is exercised only by `tests/unit/test_system_b.py` via the fake gateway. This
   120	is the intended clean seam.
