   278	
   279	## Days & rollover
   280	
   281	Rebuild on v1's staged, agent-driven model. v1's rollover is the reference
   282	(`~/.hermes/skills/productivity/rollover/`): an AGENT owns it, staged, with a brief human
   283	checkpoint. v2's current boundary is a thin deterministic slice (close yesterday with counts +
   284	one agent call that writes only the overview blurb; places no tickets, reconciles nothing).
   285	Rebuild it as the staged flow on the DB.
   286	
   287	- **DECIDED · Orchestration: one mind + the rollover skill drives it.** The staging and
   288	  reconciliation logic lives in the **skill**, not the server. Cron / autonomous path: the agent
   289	  drives it to completion. User-in-the-loop path: it drives and pauses at the human checkpoint (a
   290	  gate), then continues. The server provides only the gate + storage.
   291	- **DECIDED · Stage 1 — make the old day true: minimal now.** Work flows through the app, so
   292	  ticket statuses are already current — little to clean. **Rollover doesn't change tickets**:
   293	  tickets have their own gate (propose → approve on fields / state) and stay current as work flows
   294	  through the app, so rollover relies on that and does not touch them (it may read them for
   295	  context). FUTURE: out-of-band work the owner does elsewhere must feed back in — the only thing
   296	  that would make rollover reconcile tickets — deferred.
   297	- **DECIDED · Stage 2 — boundary mini-review (brief).** A short next-day-direction exchange, then
   298	  write the new day. Its home is **global chat** (→ *Agent runtime*). (With old-day-truth and
   299	  sprint reconciliation both handled elsewhere, rollover for now is basically this review +
   300	  writing the new day.) Sprint-item reconciliation is handled separately (→ *Sprints & sprint
   301	  items*, OPEN).
   302	- **DECIDED · Stage 3 — write the new day: not conservative.** The new day itself rides an
   303	  approval flow (agent proposes the day, owner approves), so shape it fully rather than scaffold
   304	  cautiously. Carry the right tickets forward (In Progress / still-relevant Todo / carryover;
   305	  never Done or unchosen sprint work) and write the overview.
