orchestration/tickets/T02-verify/impl-review.md:32:- Unit items are 1–21 and 36; end-to-end items are 22–35. Item 34 (snapshot migration) runs against `migration/source-snapshot/`, and item 35 (dogfood Level A) is the scripted walkthrough — both part of the suite, not manual steps. Levels B and C of the dogfood (Section 18.5) are deliberately OUTSIDE `./verify`: they use live agents and belong to stage 7's evidence, not the deterministic gate.
orchestration/tickets/T02-verify/impl-review.md:51:     7	This ticket text is also the implementation blueprint; the codex plan review runs against this file.
orchestration/tickets/T02-verify/impl-review.md:61:    17	4. Pytest invocations write junit XML to a temp/`data/`-ignored location for scoring; verify runs both suites even when the earlier suite fails (the scoreboard must always be complete), but records gate failure. A missing or unparseable junit file scores every item of that suite FAIL; verify never crashes on gate failure.
