orchestration/tickets/T02-verify/impl-review.md:506:9. Blocking: ticket blocked by an open ticket is dispatch-ineligible; blocker → `done` makes it eligible; `blocks` cycle creation rejected.
orchestration/tickets/T02-verify/impl-review.md:511:14. Claim CAS: two concurrent claim attempts on one ticket → exactly one wins, one `runs` row created.
orchestration/tickets/T02-verify/impl-review.md:513:16. Circuit breaker: two consecutive `crashed` runs → `auto_blocked`, ineligible; unblock action clears flag and counter; a `done` run resets the counter.
orchestration/tickets/T02-verify/impl-review.md:529:30. Dispatcher e2e: eligible ticket + fake spawn adapter; `POST /api/test/tick-dispatcher` claims it (run visible on Ticket); the fake worker's CLI calls (propose result with claim env) park it in `needs_review`; it appears in the approval queue; approve → `done`.
orchestration/tickets/T02-verify/impl-review.md:534:35. Dogfood Level A: `scripts/dogfood_cli.py` drives the full workflow against a test server seeded with `plan seed --demo` — agent actions through the real CLI, human actions (accepts with grant pairs, needs_review approve, day-plan decisions) through the HTTP API, since the CLI deliberately has no human verbs: create a ticket; propose and accept through every gate — every accept carrying its grant pair — including one edit-accept and one superseded proposal; write and overwrite the recap; assign to the day and remove; create a blocking link and confirm dispatch-ineligibility, then complete the blocker and confirm eligibility; claim via the test dispatcher tick; propose result with claim env; approve from needs_review to done. The script asserts each step's resulting state via `--json`/response output and exits non-zero on the first mismatch.
orchestration/tickets/T02-verify/impl-review.md:543:- **Level C — a dispatched ticket agent end to end.** Enable the real spawn adapter (config), one eligible demo ticket, real dispatcher tick: claim → run row → the spawned agent writes at least one proposal carrying the claim env → run closes with a terminal outcome and the ticket lands where its ceiling dictates. Evidence: the run row, the event sequence, and the per-run log path, all in DOGFOOD.md.
orchestration/tickets/T02-verify/impl-review.md:545:Levels B and C depend on live agent behavior: apply the three-attempt rule per level (materially different approach each time — prompt shape, ticket shaping, ceiling), and record every attempt honestly in DOGFOOD.md. Completion requires both levels' mechanical evidence. If server, CLI, or dispatcher code changes after a level's evidence was produced, that level is stale and must be re-run.
orchestration/tickets/T02-verify/impl-review.md:549:Live Hermes gateway chat; live dispatcher spawning a real agent; the final cutover seed against the live `~/.hermes/planning/` at switch time (the in-run migration proves the machinery on the frozen snapshot; the live directory will have drifted since 2026-07-04 and its import is reviewed by the human); installing skills into `~/.hermes/skills/`; launchd supervision; UI look-and-feel judgment.
orchestration/tickets/T02-verify/impl-review.md:560:249:**Build in this order**: (1) contracts skeleton — schema DDL, enums, typed models, adapter interfaces, config loading, CLI/API surface stubs; (2) **the verify instrument** (18.2), runnable with every checklist item FAIL; (3) pure-logic modules + unit tests (items 1–21 and 36) green; (4) server wiring — API, WS, resolution engine over DB, dispatcher, boundary scheduler, CLI against the API; (5) UI views; (6) Playwright e2e suite, items 22–34 green; (7) the fake-ticket dogfood pass (Section 18.5): Level A green (item 35), Levels B and C executed with evidence recorded in DOGFOOD.md. Do not start a later stage while an earlier stage's tests fail.
orchestration/tickets/T02-verify/impl-review.md:562:265:- Unit items are 1–21 and 36; end-to-end items are 22–35. Item 34 (snapshot migration) runs against `migration/source-snapshot/`, and item 35 (dogfood Level A) is the scripted walkthrough — both part of the suite, not manual steps. Levels B and C of the dogfood (Section 18.5) are deliberately OUTSIDE `./verify`: they use live agents and belong to stage 7's evidence, not the deterministic gate.
